              "login": "muhammadfawaz1"
            },
            "body": "@chaunceyjiang Closing this PR, starting the migration instead. Two things I hit that I'd rather confirm than guess:\r\n\r\nThe 4 engine-based parsers (Qwen3, MiniMax M2, Gemma4, Nemotron V3) all use explicit per-call delimiters (<function=, <invoke name=\", etc.) so the state machine knows where one tool call ends and the next begins. Hunyuan_a13b/xlam instead emit one undelimited JSON array ([{...},{...}]) — boundaries are just JSON commas/braces, no terminal token. Does the engine already support that shape, or does it need new engine-level work?\r\n\r\nHunyuan_a13b has a separate hunyuan_a13b_reasoning_parser.py (xlam doesn't). Since ParserEngine unifies reasoning + tool calls in one class, should the reasoning parser get folded in too, or stay separate?\r\n\r\n",
